  "text": {
    "suptitle": "Pooled vs stratified Shapley decomposition",
    "fig_texts": [
      "113,262 features; 22 blocks after collapsing collinearity at |rho| >= 0.9  |  REAL TARGET - dense context to SAE feature map, mlp__mean arm (#1482 single-turn corpus, 121,111 scored; covariates same corpus)",
      "Shapley sits between two endpoints by construction: a block ALONE over-counts (the set sums above the total) and its UNIQUE contribution when added last under-counts (sums below). A wide bracket means the block shares variance with others. Split-half share agreement: half1 rho=+1.000, half2 rho=+1.000. Uncertainty is split-half, not bootstrap."
    ],
